#: src/development/linux.md:21
msgid "Linkers"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:23
msgid ""
"On Linux, Rust's default linker is [LLVM's `lld`](https://blog.rust-lang."
"org/2025/09/18/Rust-1.90.0/). Alternative linkers, especially [Wild](https://"
"github.com/davidlattimore/wild) and [Mold](https://github.com/rui314/mold), "
"can improve clean and incremental build times."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:25
msgid ""
"Zed currently uses Mold in CI because it is more mature. For local "
"development, Wild is recommended because it is typically 5-20% faster than "
"Mold."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:27
msgid ""
"These linkers can be installed with `script/install-mold` and `script/"
"install-wild`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:29
msgid ""
"To use Wild as your default, add these lines to your `~/.cargo/config.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:31
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
"linker = \"clang\"\n"
"rustflags = [\"-C\", \"link-arg=--ld-path=wild\"]\n"
"\n"
"[target.aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
"linker = \"clang\"\n"
"rustflags = [\"-C\", \"link-arg=--ld-path=wild\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:41
msgid "To use Mold as your default:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:43
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[target.'cfg(target_os = \"linux\")']\n"
"rustflags = [\"-C\", \"link-arg=-fuse-ld=mold\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

